{"id": "EUVD-2026-62459", "enisaUuid": "59937c48-cbfd-3d5a-bcaf-ca1518b5550f", "description": "GitPython before 3.1.58 contains a remote code execution vulnerability in Repo.init that forwards unsafe git options without validation. Attackers can supply a template parameter pointing to a directory with malicious git hooks that execute arbitrary code when git operations are performed on the initialized repository.", "datePublished": "2026-08-19T14:02:02", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-08T15:25:00", "baseScore": 7.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/gitpython-developers/GitPython/security/advisories/GHSA-9rj7-rf2p-w77r", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/gitpython-before-remote-code-execution-via-repo-init"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-76218", "PYSEC-2026-3840", "GHSA-298h-jpq4-m665"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.83, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "b13ccbda-3f9c-33e7-a399-7389283a3088", "product": {"name": "GitPython", "vendor": {"name": "gitpython-developers"}}, "product_version": "0 <3.1.58"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "588dd9f7-8d6c-33a6-b643-9ffd22189aec", "vendor": {"name": "gitpython-developers"}}], "isExploited": false}